{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvpvZwti3L1VTf3kwjk2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The paper draft is written and compiles, but the full validation gate did not run locally. `pdftotext` is missing, so `compile_latex.sh` stopped. The figure validator also failed on an import error (`No module named 'src'`). I compiled with plain `pdflatex`/`bibtex` instead, so the orchestrator's compile and page-fill check are still needed.\n\nWhat does pass: the claims validator (18 claims, 28 references) and the scientific-evidence verifier (77 links, 0 dangling).\n\n**What the paper says**\n- **Thesis:** accuracy of regression-based GATE estimation is governed by how well the fitted exposure mapping matches the true mechanism, not by graph family, interference strength or assignment design within the tested range.\n- **Final result:** the sealed final evaluation is `qualified`, on 24 unseen seeds across 8 cases. The frozen estimator scores a mean relative RMSE of 0.126, against 0.180 for plain linear regression, 0.622 for difference-in-means, 0.994 for Horvitz–Thompson and 0.045 for the oracle.\n- **Per-case error:** 0.031–0.054 in the five cases where the mapping matches, and 0.151–0.452 in the saturating, count×degree and two-hop cases.\n- **Negative results:** the nominal 95% intervals cover only 0.839. The two-hop case is unresolved and its cause is unknown (gate diagnostics were not verified). The flexible ridge ensemble and the linear-plus-correction variant did not beat plain linear on the 8 model-selection seeds.\n- **Limitations stated in the paper:** case specifications are shared between model selection and final scoring, and the gate and library were not ablated. It also covers one graph size, case-pair contrasts without per-case intervals, no public-graph experiments, and qualification as a statement about this grid only.\n\n**Page budget:** the body runs to 9 pages. With the placeholder